WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.330 --> 00:00:06.330
So that about wraps us up. Thanks very much for watching everyone, I think that takes us to the end.

2
00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:10.330
Obviously for all of this stuff you can find out more detail on the Unreal documentation.

3
00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:17.329
On Unreal YouTube there's live streams about new features, talks from various developers actually working on the engine themselves.

4
00:00:17.329 --> 00:00:19.329
Same thing for the Twitch streams.

5
00:00:19.329 --> 00:00:23.329
Unreal Developer Network is available to anyone who's an Unreal Engine licensee.

6
00:00:23.329 --> 00:00:26.329
For anyone who isn't a licensee we also have the AnswerHub.

7
00:00:26.329 --> 00:00:35.329
Epic recently announced a new category of answer that is pulling some of the highest traffic answered questions from the UDN.

8
00:00:35.329 --> 00:00:40.329
So from real licensee dev scenarios and bringing them over into the AnswerHub.

9
00:00:40.329 --> 00:00:43.329
So the rest of the community can see those, so that's very exciting.

10
00:00:43.329 --> 00:00:46.329
And last off we have the Unreal Engine Community Wiki.

11
00:00:46.329 --> 00:00:50.329
Which is basically where the community could be uploading tutorials and documentation.

12
00:00:50.329 --> 00:00:56.329
The only thing to mention there is that some of those solutions may not always be the most efficient.

13
00:00:56.329 --> 00:00:58.329
And may be slightly out of date.

14
00:00:58.329 --> 00:01:03.329
They don't have the same kind of burden and requirement of keeping these things up to date as Epic's own materials do.

15
00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:08.329
But all of these are fantastic resources and peruse them at your own leisure.

16
00:01:08.329 --> 00:01:12.329
Thanks very much for watching everyone and I hope you have a great rest of your day.
